{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787026537905311001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"slowmoving-engaging-kouprey","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7e329513e807b36e8e46e37660a821f68d661eb296473369914d85fb37ea6f58","event_uuid":"eb538b59-2b03-4364-bdd2-6cb769de0531","position":{"commit_sha":"cc7a50ca92ca5e61d0afc3e0c8c14d1cc81d8c5e","position":"1787022577489555001-eb538b59-2b03-4364-bdd2-6cb769de0531"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a54b61a88e22fc2360f55117feecb7fd94bb645f86710e93df2e0641e8eb6a49","event_uuid":"90827a02-e9ff-4e1d-94b9-03e0f29d9fc8","position":{"commit_sha":"1e697b33703ef4e13711975536c42010aee4f55e","position":"1787022676960570001-90827a02-e9ff-4e1d-94b9-03e0f29d9fc8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"eb37e552abb1eb5a59a496cf73757476e1d1d9e95d9ea5ddfa74465f887886c5","event_uuid":"811b15e9-6b19-4e69-8d1a-55f7f1c02e46","position":{"commit_sha":"8423ed2aa7b5f791f592ae6cd21326ff3f849f23","position":"1787022766790660001-811b15e9-6b19-4e69-8d1a-55f7f1c02e46"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"678ee286b0f0712e12e4d25b91fcfacff8a0cbff6ea99c3745bb71e2ea3245a7","event_uuid":"d22054a5-b373-4a37-8ddd-d0067867abb3","position":{"commit_sha":"9ea5d38c6e0158a2c227b051e9c94677d79fbd80","position":"1787022919148552001-d22054a5-b373-4a37-8ddd-d0067867abb3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7d9cb0889ec1ef7e7c635360be2f3601df34b011f28443d93903359d7a7ef2f5","event_uuid":"98ebb4c0-5d4d-4bc1-b5d8-b758cf6d4c47","position":{"commit_sha":"1f4008be70f4d388381f107091f4e380da02efb9","position":"1787023016604626001-98ebb4c0-5d4d-4bc1-b5d8-b758cf6d4c47"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787022577489555001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"90827a02-e9ff-4e1d-94b9-03e0f29d9fc8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f828-6f5e-3b15-41f5"},{"link_uuid":"811b15e9-6b19-4e69-8d1a-55f7f1c02e46","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nS1 proves one atomic update executor and S2 produces pure plans, but legacy batch dispatch still replays compound methods, conflates deferred and applied work, and uses a rolling breaker that cannot distinguish physical attempts from exhausted logical outcomes. One ticket-local or permanent failure can distort batch behavior.\n\n## Outcome\nMake the typed coordinator authoritative for non-create plans: update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict handling. Execute atomic desired postconditions in dependency order; after partial success, re-observe and plan only remaining drift. Produce exact ticket/pass outcomes and apply the approved endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse only to normalized exhausted logical failures.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a coordinator that consumes immutable plans, enforces dependencies, and calls adapter atomic operations through S1s budget. Preserve successful earlier postconditions and never replay the whole compound mutation after a late failure.\n2. Normalize auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, and skipped dispositions with ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global scope.\n3. Replace the rolling 5-of-10 breaker. Endpoint scope opens after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across at least two tickets; provider scope additionally spans two endpoint families. A matching success resets consecutive state.\n4. Exclude physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404, and opaque diagnostics from inferred fuse counters. Retain direct authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, and global behavior.\n5. When a fuse opens, defer remaining matching plans with reason/scope/retry metadata while independent scopes continue. Preserve exact applied/failed/deferred/skipped tallies and nonzero degraded-pass signaling.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- Coordinator tables cover dependency success/failure, partial compound update, idempotent already-gone delete, ticket-local 404 isolation, permanent 4xx, auth/quota/rate scopes, and mixed endpoint families.\n- Fuse sequences assert threshold, two-ticket/two-family requirements, success reset, exclusions, and independent-scope continuation.\n- Replay fixtures derived from historical GitHub Actions outcomes assert zero premature stop in the completed 1,200-run slice; raw warning/grep text is never classified as a terminal outcome.\n- Verified-fake Cloud/DC batches assert wire order, maximum calls, exact tallies, logs, and exit status.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nCut over by non-create operation family and never dual-send. Before legacy removal, an operation-family flag can select the old dispatcher. Rollback preserves successful Jira effects and resumes from re-observation. The intentional differences are three-call shared budgeting, explicit deferral, exact partial outcomes, and replacement of the rolling breaker.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Non-create plans execute atomic postconditions once in dependency order; a late failure preserves earlier success and re-observes only remaining drift within the same logical budget.\n- [ ] Ticket-local/permanent failures isolate the ticket, authoritative broad scopes stop only their declared scope, and independent tickets/endpoints continue.\n- [ ] Endpoint fuse opens only after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across two tickets; provider fuse additionally requires two endpoint families; matching success resets state.\n- [ ] Physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, and opaque diagnostics never increment inferred fuse counters.\n- [ ] Remaining matching work is explicitly deferred with reason/scope/`retry_not_before`; applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Historical replay fixtures and verified-fake Cloud/DC batches show no premature termination of observed successful/partially successful work.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/coordinator.py","reason":"Typed per-ticket non-create operation coordinator."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/failure_policy.py","reason":"Provider-neutral failure scope and disposition policy."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_fuse.py","reason":"Approved endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"Route non-create operations to the coordinator."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"Retire compound replay and preserve exact batch outcomes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Execute one plan with dependency and partial-postcondition accounting."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"Carry deferral, fuse, and exact phase outcomes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py","reason":"Non-create dependency, partial success, scope, and tally tables."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py","reason":"Threshold, reset, exclusion, and independent-scope sequences."},{"path":"tests/fixtures/reconciler/rp03_fuse_completed_slice.json","reason":"Sanitized historical outcome replay fixture."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","f828-6f5e-3b15-41f5"],["parent","4217-d1d6-370b-4e98"],["relates_to","6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp03","reconciler","jira","reliability","tdd"],"ticket_id":"28a3-a62d-6345-44a0","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-03 S3 — Coordinate non-create operations with deferral and the scoped fuse","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Non-create coordinator dependencies, partial postconditions, scope, fuse, and exact tallies"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_retry.py","dd_id":"AC2-AC4","dd_text":"Ticket-local 404 and permanent-failure isolation regressions"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py -k historical","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Sanitized historical replay and verified-fake Cloud/DC batch behavior"}]},"source_event_uuids":["eb538b59-2b03-4364-bdd2-6cb769de0531","90827a02-e9ff-4e1d-94b9-03e0f29d9fc8","811b15e9-6b19-4e69-8d1a-55f7f1c02e46","d22054a5-b373-4a37-8ddd-d0067867abb3","98ebb4c0-5d4d-4bc1-b5d8-b758cf6d4c47"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787026537905311001,"uuid":"edd677b5-99e7-4539-8fef-8a1ce75d37a8"}